---
import PageFrame from "../components/PageFrame.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Support Logos AI"
  description="Support Logos AI with GitHub Sponsors, Buy Me a Coffee, or paid setup help for installs, voices, Ollama, and API.Bible guidance."
>
  <PageFrame current="support">
    <main class="shell py-16">
      <section class="max-w-4xl animate-rise">
        <p class="eyebrow">Support Logos AI</p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 section-title">Back the project or let me handle the setup.</h1>
        <p class="mt-6 section-copy">
          If Logos AI is useful to you, the simplest ways to help are recurring support, one-time support, or a paid
          setup plan. Self-serve docs stay open either way. Support goes toward development, releases, docs, and the
          time it takes to keep the app improving across web, desktop, CLI, and TUI.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
          <a href="https://github.com/sponsors/jd4rider" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="cta-primary">
            Support on GitHub Sponsors
          </a>
          <a href="https://buymeacoffee.com/jd4rider" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="cta-secondary">
            Buy Me a Coffee
          </a>
          <a href="https://docs.logos-ai.online" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="cta-secondary">
            Read setup docs
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <article class="surface-card p-8">
          <p class="eyebrow">Recurring Support</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl text-text">GitHub Sponsors</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">
            Best fit for people who want to support the project long term, follow development in public, and back the
            open-source side of Logos AI directly from GitHub.
          </p>
          <a href="https://github.com/sponsors/jd4rider" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="mt-6 inline-flex cta-primary">
            Open GitHub Sponsors
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="surface-card p-8">
          <p class="eyebrow">One-Time Support</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl text-text">Buy Me a Coffee</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">
            Best fit for casual support, quick thank-you payments, and people who want the fastest way to chip in
            without thinking about tiers or GitHub accounts.
          </p>
          <a href="https://buymeacoffee.com/jd4rider" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="mt-6 inline-flex cta-secondary">
            Open Buy Me a Coffee
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="surface-card p-8">
          <p class="eyebrow">Paid Setup Help</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl text-text">Done-for-you guidance</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">
            If you want help getting the full environment working, I can handle install planning, voice setup,
            Ollama, and guided API.Bible configuration as a paid service.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col gap-3 text-sm text-muted">
            <a href="mailto:jd4rider@gmail.com" class="nav-link">Email: jd4rider@gmail.com</a>
            <a href="tel:+14063967246" class="nav-link">Call or text: 406-396-7246</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr]">
        <div class="surface-card p-8">
          <p class="eyebrow">What setup help can cover</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl text-text">From install to a working study desk.</h2>
          <ul class="mt-5 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">
            <li>Install the desktop app, CLI, or TUI on macOS, Windows, or Linux</li>
            <li>Set up Ollama for local AI commentary and Logos Chat</li>
            <li>Install Kokoro or Piper for better read-aloud voices</li>
            <li>Guide API.Bible app creation and key placement</li>
            <li>Help choose a simple path between free, BYOK, and future managed options</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="surface-card p-8">
          <p class="eyebrow">Important Note</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl text-text">Support, not tax-deductible charity.</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">
            These support links are for backing development and setup work. They should be treated as support for the
            project, not as tax-deductible charitable donations.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
            <a href="/download" class="cta-secondary">Download app</a>
            <a href="/pricing" class="cta-secondary">View product pricing</a>
            <a href="https://docs.logos-ai.online/getting-started/desktop-install/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="cta-secondary">
              Install docs
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
  </PageFrame>
</SiteLayout>
